the Clark County School District is  mourning the loss of a teacher who was a  real Trailblazer when it came to music  Albert Avia had a passion for music and  education he helped launch ccsd's  Mariachi Azul and taught at Fremont  Middle School and tonight Christian  Garcia spoke to his widow about the  music teacher and how she's now working  to fulfill a dream  it's been weeks since Albert Avila  passed away his wife Julie Gathering her  strength to share his story after a  sudden stomach pain forced the couple to  rush to the hospital ultimately losing  his life during an intestinal rupture  some days are good  actually I should say some moments are  good  um  most moments aren't Avila says the 39  year old school teacher was a staple  with the Clark County School District  helping launch Mariachi education across  the state of Nevada he worked really  hard a lot of the time to make sure that  mariachi music wasn't just looked at as  a novelty that it it had the same faces  as Jazz as band as orchestras choir  eight news now highlighting his work  during this year's Hispanic heritage  celebration I love it I love hearing it  I love seeing the passion that they grow  for as members of the Mariachi Azul from  Fremont Middle School showed off their  skills foreign  expressing our culture today the  mariachi music education program is the  largest in the country the group was  recently selected to represent Las Vegas  at the Midwest clinic conference in  Chicago a dream Avila was hoping to  perform at to help grow the music  program and show other band directors  Orchestra choir directors that they  couldn't create this program to connect  to those students  public funeral service schedule for  November 12th at 8 in the morning at St  Christopher Catholic Church which is in  North Las Vegas now the students are  raising money for that music conference  in Chicago they have set up a donation  page and we have posted it so you can  share it on 8newsnow.com
 

